## AUDIT AREA 1 — JOB REQUISITION WORKFLOW

### 1.1 Current Implementation

```mermaid
graph LR
    A["HR Opens ATSScanner.tsx"] --> B["Fills Job Title + JD Text"]
    B --> C["AI Generates Form Schema"]
    C --> D["Clicks 'Publish Form'"]
    D --> E["INSERT into job_forms"]
    E --> F["Public Link Generated"]
```

**Parallel Pathway (CareerPortal.tsx + CandidateMessages.tsx):**
```mermaid
graph LR
    A2["HR Opens CareerPortal.tsx"] --> B2["Fills Job Details"]
    B2 --> C2["INSERT into recruitment_posts"]
    C2 --> D2["Visible on Candidate Careers Page"]
```

### 1.2 Critical Workflow Flaws

| # | Flaw | Severity | Enterprise Standard |
|---|------|----------|-------------------|
| WF-01 | **No job requisition approval workflow** — HR creates and publishes jobs directly without manager, department head, or finance approval | **Critical** | Workday: Requisition → Manager → Finance → VP → HR Publish |
| WF-02 | **No hiring manager ownership** — No `hiring_manager_id` exists on any job table | **Critical** | Every requisition must have a named hiring manager who owns the pipeline |
| WF-03 | **No budget validation** — Jobs are created without headcount or salary band checks | **High** | Requisitions require approved headcount and budget allocation |
| WF-04 | **No department approval** — Department head is never consulted | **High** | Department leads must approve headcount additions |
| WF-05 | **Two parallel job creation pathways** — `job_forms` (ATSScanner) and `recruitment_posts` (CareerPortal/CandidateMessages) are independent systems | **Critical** | Single unified job entity with lifecycle states |
| WF-06 | **No job status lifecycle** — `job_forms` has only `status: 'Active'`; `recruitment_posts` has only `Open/Closed` | **High** | Required: `Draft → Pending Approval → Approved → Published → Paused → Closed → Archived` |
| WF-07 | **No expiration date** — Jobs remain active indefinitely | **Medium** | Auto-close after 30/60/90 days configurable |
| WF-08 | **No headcount tracking** — Cannot specify how many positions to fill per requisition | **High** | Must track `openings_total` vs `openings_filled` |
| WF-09 | **JD generated in-memory only** — [Recruitment.tsx L92](file:///c:/Users/veere/Downloads/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/flowtracker/src/pages/hr/Recruitment.tsx#L92) stores JD in React state, not persisted to database | **High** | JD must be versioned and linked to requisition |
| WF-10 | **No audit trail** — No record of who created/modified/approved a job | **Critical** | Every state change must be logged with actor + timestamp |

### 1.3 Recommended Enterprise Workflow

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Draft: Hiring Manager creates requisition
    Draft --> PendingDeptApproval: Submit for approval
    PendingDeptApproval --> PendingFinanceApproval: Dept Head approves
    PendingDeptApproval --> Draft: Dept Head rejects (with comments)
    PendingFinanceApproval --> Approved: Finance validates budget
    PendingFinanceApproval --> Draft: Budget rejected
    Approved --> Published: HR publishes to career portal
    Published --> Paused: HR temporarily pauses intake
    Paused --> Published: HR resumes
    Published --> Closed: All positions filled OR manual close
    Closed --> Archived: After retention period
```

