## AUDIT AREA 3 — CANDIDATE APPLICATION WORKFLOW

### 3.1 Current Implementation (End-to-End Trace)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Candidate
    participant JP as JobApplication.tsx
    participant DB as Supabase DB
    
    C->>JP: Opens /apply/{formId}
    JP->>DB: SELECT job_forms WHERE id = formId
    JP->>JP: Render dynamic form
    C->>JP: Fills form + uploads resume
    JP->>DB: SELECT candidates WHERE email = input
    alt Candidate exists
        JP->>DB: UPDATE candidates SET stage
    else New candidate
        JP->>DB: INSERT INTO candidates
    end
    JP->>DB: UPLOAD resume to storage bucket
    JP->>DB: INSERT INTO job_applications
    JP->>DB: INSERT INTO candidate_applications
    JP->>DB: UPDATE candidates SET stage = 'Applied'
    
    Note over JP,DB: 4 sequential writes with NO transaction
```

### 3.2 Critical Workflow Flaws

| # | Flaw | Severity | Impact |
|---|------|----------|--------|
| WF-17 | **Triple-write without transaction** — Writes to `candidates`, `job_applications`, and `candidate_applications` sequentially. If any fails, data drifts | **Critical** | Application exists in one table but not others |
| WF-18 | **Can a candidate apply to multiple jobs?** — Partially. The candidate record's `stage` field is globally overwritten per application, losing previous job's stage | **Critical** | Candidate at "Offer" stage for Job A gets reset to "Applied" when applying for Job B |
| WF-19 | **Can a candidate apply to the same job twice?** — **Yes** — The `candidate_applications` table has a unique constraint that catches duplicates via error code `23505` in [ATSScanner.tsx L369](file:///c:/Users/veere/Downloads/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/flowtracker/src/pages/hr/recruitment/ATSScanner.tsx#L369), but [JobApplication.tsx](file:///c:/Users/veere/Downloads/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/flowtracker/src/pages/public/JobApplication.tsx) has **no such check** | **High** | Duplicate applications from career portal are silently created |
| WF-20 | **Candidate cannot track their own applications** — The candidate dashboard ([CandidateDashboard.tsx](file:///c:/Users/veere/Downloads/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/flowtracker/src/pages/candidate/Dashboard.tsx)) shows BGC docs and assessments, but has **zero application tracking** | **Critical** | Candidates have no visibility into their pipeline status |
| WF-21 | **No reusable candidate profile** — Each application via [JobApplication.tsx](file:///c:/Users/veere/Downloads/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/flowtracker/src/pages/public/JobApplication.tsx) is standalone. There is no "My Profile" pre-fill | **High** | Candidates re-enter name, email, phone for every application |
| WF-22 | **No application withdrawal** — Candidates cannot withdraw an active application | **High** | Required for compliance (GDPR right to erasure) |
| WF-23 | **No application status notifications** — No email/in-app notification when status changes | **High** | Enterprise ATS sends notifications at every stage transition |

