## AUDIT AREA 15 — SCALABILITY RISKS

### 15.1 Workflow Bottlenecks at Scale (5000 Candidates / 100 Recruiters)

| Bottleneck | Current Impact | At Scale Impact |
|-----------|---------------|----------------|
| `select('*')` on all applications without pagination | All rows loaded in browser | **Browser crash at 50k+ rows** |
| Sequential AI calls in ATSScanner (4s delay between candidates) | Acceptable for 5 candidates | **5.5 hours for 5000 candidates** |
| Sequential AI calls in PerformanceEngine | Acceptable for 10 employees | **1.1 hours for 1000 employees** |
| No index on `candidate_applications(candidate_id, job_form_id)` | Acceptable at low volume | **Full table scan on every duplicate check** |
| Client-side join in ApplicationHub | 100ms for 50 records | **5+ seconds for 5000 records** |
| Realtime channels per component | 5 channels for 1 user | **500 channels for 100 concurrent recruiters** |
| No connection pooling configured | Acceptable for 10 users | **Connection exhaustion at 100+ concurrent users** |

### 15.2 Recommended Scalability Architecture

1. **Server-side pagination** — Cursor-based for all list views
2. **Batch AI processing** — Queue system for bulk resume scanning (10 concurrent, not sequential)
3. **Database views for dashboards** — Pre-aggregated metrics instead of client-side computation
4. **Shared realtime channel manager** — Multiplex all updates through a single channel per user
5. **Background job queue** — Supabase Edge Functions with async processing for AI tasks
6. **Redis cache layer** — For dashboard counts and frequently-accessed metadata

